<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH FIRST DEPUTY FINMIN LEAVES END-AUGUST.</title>
<headline>CZECH FIRST DEPUTY FINMIN LEAVES END-AUGUST.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech first deputy finance minister Jan Klak is to leave his job at the end of August and hopes to work in the private sector, CTK nwes agency reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>Klak, who was responsible for taxes and customs, is to be replaced by Michal Frankl of the Civic democratic Alliance (ODA), CTK said.</p>
